   "Date taken from the print code EIGI-05.2-FG(HB) next to the reference number in the footer (no other date printed).",
   "Daylight exposure, E-6/CR-56, Status A. x axis of curves is log H in lux-seconds as printed. RMS granularity 8: gross diffuse visual density 1.0, 48 um aperture.",
   "curves: r solid, g dash-dot, b dashed. Unlike Velvia 50, r stays below g and b throughout (no crossing). g and b differ by about 0.1 on the shoulder (D above 2.7), then run so close that their dashes share one ink band from log H about -1.7 to -1.25 (separated by 0.03 in the hints only; the trace may not tell them apart there); below log H -1.25 all three coincide within about 0.02 and are traced alike. The curves end at log H 1.0 (frame edge), D-min plateau about 0.134.",
   "sensitivity: y is relative log sensitivity as printed (sensitivity = reciprocal of the exposure in J/cm2 giving the specified density, which the sheet states as 1.0 above D-min). Curves are drawn only between about -0.7 and the peak on each side, from 395-522 nm (b), 482-602 nm (g), 550-690 nm (r); the trace is on a 5 nm grid, so the last 0-4 nm at each end are cut.",
